  "details": "I want to make a remote control that responds to joystick inputs while it's being held -- but it would be confusing if someone picked up the remote in their left hand but had to operate it with their right joystick.   I could make it listen to BOTH joysticks, but then they would have none left to navigate with.   So, I want to be able to know (in Udon) which hand the pickup is being held in, so that I can decide to respond to only those inputs;  it could be either as an argument to OnPickup, or just as a property that an Udon script can look at.   Is there any way to do this?",
